From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Domenico D'Arrigo <DCHEM88@hotmail.it>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 21:37:46 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 3/6] LvglLib: Style the stock widgets from LvglTheme.h

Drop-downs, text areas, check boxes, buttons and lists get their look
from LVGL's default theme, which lv_display_create() initializes in
light mode with LVGL's blue and red. On a dark LvglTheme.h they stay
white. Initialize the default theme again from new LvglTheme.h macros:
primary and secondary color and dark mode, with the scaled body font.
The defaults are LVGL's own values, so the look does not change unless
the theme sets them.

Co-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018n3yuWwDLW63F4vdf7ZFTv
---
 Include/LvglTheme.h       | 12 ++++++++++++
 Library/LvglLib/LvglLib.c | 14 ++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 26 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Include/LvglTheme.h b/Include/LvglTheme.h
index 3d081b1..3120324 100644
--- a/Include/LvglTheme.h
+++ b/Include/LvglTheme.h
@@ -58,6 +58,18 @@
 //
 #define THEME_ACCENT_PALETTE      LV_PALETTE_BLUE
 
+//
+// Stock LVGL widgets (drop-downs, text areas, check boxes, buttons, lists)
+// are styled by LVGL's default theme, which LvglLib initializes with:
+//   primary   -- focus outline, checked / selected fill, button background
+//   secondary -- LVGL's secondary accent
+//   dark      -- 1: dark widget surfaces with light text, 0: light ones
+// The values below are LVGL's own defaults (blue, red, light).
+//
+#define THEME_COLOR_WIDGET_PRIMARY    0x2196F3
+#define THEME_COLOR_WIDGET_SECONDARY  0xF44336
+#define THEME_WIDGETS_DARK            0
+
 //
 // Fonts -- must be enabled in lv_conf.h. Sizes scale with UiScale via
 // LvglThemeFont*() (base: title 20, body/popup 16).
diff --git a/Library/LvglLib/LvglLib.c b/Library/LvglLib/LvglLib.c
index c6ba451..9ee3a2a 100644
--- a/Library/LvglLib/LvglLib.c
+++ b/Library/LvglLib/LvglLib.c
@@ -4,6 +4,7 @@
 #include <Library/LvglLib.h>
 #include <Library/LvglUiConfigLib.h>
 #include <Library/LvglThemeLib.h>
+#include <LvglTheme.h>
 
 extern UINT8  mExitBtnYes;
 
@@ -90,6 +91,19 @@ UefiLvglInit (
     return EFI_UNSUPPORTED;
   }
 
+  //
+  // LVGL's default theme styles the stock widgets (drop-downs, text areas,
+  // check boxes, buttons, lists): take its colors and light/dark mode from
+  // LvglTheme.h, so that they match the chrome drawn by the renderer.
+  //
+  lv_theme_default_init (
+    Display,
+    lv_color_hex (THEME_COLOR_WIDGET_PRIMARY),
+    lv_color_hex (THEME_COLOR_WIDGET_SECONDARY),
+    THEME_WIDGETS_DARK,
+    LvglThemeFontBody ()
+    );
+
   lv_port_indev_init(Display);
 
   mUefiLvglInitDone = TRUE;
